  "content": {
    "id": "p12-q40-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "40",
    "prompt": "In the expansion of $(4+x)^n$, the coefficient of $x^7$ is twice the coefficient of $x^8$. Find the value of $n$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$n=23$.\n\nUse $\\binom{n}{7}4^{n-7}=2\\binom{n}{8}4^{n-8}$.",
      "worked": "The general term is $T_k=\\binom{n}{k}4^{n-k}x^k$. The stated coefficient relationship gives\n$$\\begin{align*}\\binom{n}{7}4^{n-7}&=2\\binom{n}{8}4^{n-8}\\\\4\\binom{n}{7}&=2\\binom{n}{8}\\\\4\\frac{n!}{7!(n-7)!}&=2\\frac{n!}{8!(n-8)!}\\\\4\\times8!(n-8)!&=2\\times7!(n-7)!\\\\32&=2(n-7)\\\\n-7&=16\\\\n&=23.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 68
  },
